### ============================================================
### Vitrine 3D — End-to-End Registration & Auth Flow
### Compatible with: IntelliJ IDEA HTTP Client / VS Code REST Client
### ============================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@contentType = application/json

### ============================================================
### STEP 1 — Register a new store owner
### ============================================================
### Run this first. After success (201), copy the returned "id"
### and set it in the @storeId variable below (step 3).
### ============================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/register
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "teste@vitrine3d.com",
  "password": "senha123",
  "userName": "Henrique Dev",
  "storeName": "Minha Loja 3D",
  "whatsappNumber": "5511999999999",
  "storeDescription": "Loja especializada em impressão 3D de alta qualidade.",
  "stateId": 1,
  "cityId": 1
}

### ============================================================
### STEP 2 — Login and obtain JWT token
### ============================================================
### IntelliJ: the response handler script below automatically
### captures the token into the client global variable "authToken".
###
### VS Code REST Client: manually copy the "token" value from
### the response body and paste it into @authToken below (step 3).
### ============================================================

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: {{contentType}}

{
  "email": "teste@vitrine3d.com",
  "password": "senha123"
}

> {%
  // IntelliJ HTTP Client — captures token automatically after login
  client.global.set("authToken", response.body.token);
  client.global.set("storeId", response.body.id);
  client.log("Token captured: " + response.body.token);
  client.log("Store ID captured: " + response.body.id);
%}

### ============================================================
### STEP 3 — Upload store logo (multipart/form-data)
### ============================================================
### Prerequisites:
###   - IntelliJ: token and storeId are set automatically by step 2.
###   - VS Code: set @authToken and @storeId manually below.
###
### Replace the file path in the logo part with a real image on
### your machine (JPG or PNG recommended, max ~5 MB).
### ============================================================

@authToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzUxMiJ9.eyJzdWIiOiJ0ZXN0ZUB2aXRyaW5lM2QuY29tIiwiaWF0IjoxNzgxNTI2NzY4LCJleHAiOjE3ODE2MTMxNjh9.YpHRH3VMICqlHtD0wcvKkHSt4aM0dOWzV0pQNDweFyFizO3fAzeJyqp6K-IpPDbZWNocD4KDXeeNYNHkLeQWjw
@storeId   = 1

POST {{baseUrl}}/api/users/{{storeId}}/logo
Authorization: Bearer {{authToken}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=----Boundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW

------Boundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="logo"; filename="logo.png"
Content-Type: image/png

< ./logo.png
------Boundary7MA4YWxkTrZu0gW--
